# Summary

cross-cluster-generator.ts §2.5 drift-driven path (lines 466-497) pairs the drifted entity with EVERY member of target_cluster_id in other components. No cap. The §2.2 sweep has MAX_CANDIDATES_PER_COMPONENT_PAIR=5; the §2.5 path has nothing equivalent.

A drift event with target_cluster_id pointing at a 500-member cluster yields up to ~500 candidate rows for a single drifted entity. The reconciliation_agent processes merge_candidates serially in its prompt-builder loop, so a runaway drift event blows out the agent's prompt budget and crowds out other candidates' attention.

# Decision (locked 2026-05-21)

Option (a) per-drift-event cap: top-N by score. New env knob MAX_DRIFT_DRIVEN_CANDIDATES_PER_EVENT, default 10. Mirrors §2.2's MAX_CANDIDATES_PER_COMPONENT_PAIR pattern.

Rejected:
- (b) Apply BRIDGE_SCORE_THRESHOLD to drift-driven rows — violates doc §2.5's locked 'drift-driven rows always insert' semantics.
- (c) No cap; document the unbounded fan-out as intentional — leaves a real operational footgun. Cluster sizes are not controlled by Mnemo; an HDBSCAN run that produces one large cluster (legitimate signal-rich domain) becomes a denial-of-attention vector for the reconciliation_agent.

The top-N preserves the 'always insert' intent — the strongest N candidates per drift event still always insert, bypassing the BRIDGE_SCORE_THRESHOLD that §2.2 enforces. The cap bounds blast radius without changing the doc-locked semantics.

